    "source": "eureka-valley-context-statement",
    "note": "Named among the properties associated with the social and political life of the district as the home of Henry Becker, who led the Eureka Valley Improvement Association for ten consecutive terms from 1910 until 1927, and put forward as possibly eligible for the California Register on that association. The statement records the house as a rear lot house behind 536 Castro Street; the city carries the parcel as 534-536 Castro Street."
